{"event": "sample", "boot": 0, "arm": "current", "case": "short-1", "input_tokens": 27, "wall_s": 4.281, "decode_tps": 51.262, "text": "A refrigerator operates by utilizing a refrigerant, a fluid with a low boiling point, to transfer thermal energy from the interior to the exterior. Inside the refrigerator, the refrigerant flows through coils where it absorbs heat from the food and air, causing it to evaporate and turn into a gas. This process lowers the temperature inside the compartment, effectively removing heat from the stored items. The warm, low-pressure gas is then drawn into a compressor, which increases its pressure and temperature significantly, preparing it for the next stage of the cycle.\n\nOnce compressed, the hot, high-pressure gas moves to the condenser coils located on the outside of the refrigerator, typically at the back or bottom. Here, the refrigerant releases its absorbed heat into the surrounding room air, causing it to condense back into a liquid. This liquid then passes through an expansion valve, which drops its pressure and temperature, allowing it to return to the interior coils to absorb more heat.", "ids": [32, 43447, 25224, 539, 33731, 264, 28417, 505, 11, 264, 15133, 440, 264, 3238, 48161, 1406, 11, 310, 8059, 27462, 4649, 494, 279, 14362, 310, 279, 26383, 13, 26482, 279, 43447, 11, 279, 28417, 505, 26565, 1472, 68366, 1332, 424, 86914, 8364, 494, 279, 3487, 321, 3594, 11, 13969, 424, 310, 57054, 344, 321, 2404, 1083, 264, 6605, 13, 1061, 1817, 69569, 279, 9039, 4613, 279, 42060, 11, 13057, 17068, 8364, 494, 279, 9476, 3470, 13, 561, 7948, 11, 3238, 85416, 6605, 369, 1179, 14336, 1083, 264, 56885, 11, 864, 12339, 1141, 7035, 321, 9039, 11602, 11, 19435, 424, 364, 279, 1727, 6228, 314, 279, 10458, 13, 271, 12162, 29648, 11, 279, 3882, 11, 1496, 85416, 6605, 10480, 310, 279, 9464, 57438, 68366, 7172, 383, 279, 4732, 314, 279, 43447, 11, 10813, 506, 279, 1142, 466, 5445, 13, 5514, 11, 279, 28417, 505, 18652, 1141, 39647, 8364, 1083, 279,